# The Core Problem

Enterprise applications like:

* Lingo
* SAMX
* BNE
* Basics

are very complex.

Users are usually only trained on the “happy path”:

* click this button
* upload this file
* follow these steps

But when something unexpected happens:

* zip code validation fails
* census API goes down
* rates don’t load
* data mismatches occur
* backend services fail
* installation errors happen

users don’t know what to do. 

That creates:

* repeated support tickets
* manual DevOps intervention
* wasted engineering time
* delays in onboarding/workflows
* poor user experience

---

# Your Proposed Solution

The idea is to build an AI-powered assistant embedded into the application UI and backend workflows.

The assistant can:

### 1. Detect Errors

Monitor:

* frontend validation failures
* backend service failures
* batch job failures
* API outages
* production defects
* runtime issues

Example:

> “This zip code is unsupported”
> “Plan API is unavailable”
> “Census validation failed”



---

### 2. Recommend Fixes Automatically

Using historical defect logs + past resolutions, the model suggests solutions like:

> “This issue usually happens when the census extractor service is down.”
> “Try refreshing after deployment completes.”
> “Your parameter configuration appears invalid.”

The idea is basically:

* build a knowledge base from previous incidents
* train/retrieve from historical defect data
* guide users in real time



---

### 3. Predict Issues Before They Happen

One interesting part mentioned:

The system could proactively warn users before submission failures happen.

Example:

> “This ZIP code historically fails validation.”
> “This configuration often causes installation failures.”

That turns the assistant from reactive → predictive. 

